WEBVTT

00:35.334 --> 00:36.710
All right, all bets are in.

00:36.836 --> 00:39.504
Rupert, bad idea trusting the Celtics.

00:39.630 --> 00:42.134
Worse than when I trusted Brian
to pack my parachute.

00:56.858 --> 01:00.905
<i>Hey, Brian, care to place a wager?
Tomorrow night on Fox's Celebrity Boxing,</i>

01:01.030 --> 01:03.866
I've got Carol Channing beating
Mike Tyson in three rounds.

01:03.949 --> 01:04.994
Carol Channing.

01:05.077 --> 01:09.165
You've got Carol Channing, the actress,
beating Mike Tyson, the boxer.

01:09.290 --> 01:12.209
- Hell, give me $50 on Tyson.
- Well, you're in good company.

01:12.293 --> 01:13.961
Betting Freddy took the same wager.

01:14.045 --> 01:17.089
Bet!

01:17.381 --> 01:20.678
Wait a minute.
There's nothing funny about an addiction.

01:20.845 --> 01:23.139
Vote no on Indian gaming laws.

01:26.350 --> 01:28.854
<i>And we're back with
Fox Celebrity Boxing</i>

01:28.979 --> 01:30.897
<i>with Mike Tyson and Carol Channing.</i>

01:30.980 --> 01:33.817
I tell you, Jim, how Carol Channing
outlasted that barrage

01:33.901 --> 01:35.527
in the second round, we'll never know.

01:39.408 --> 01:42.035
Come here, young man.
I'm gonna bop you one.

01:46.498 --> 01:49.252
- She's getting beat!
- No, she's getting mad.

01:50.044 --> 01:51.963
You ain't so tough, young man.

01:54.424 --> 01:58.053
That all you got, you son of a bitch?
You're going down, young man.

02:02.433 --> 02:03.976
You're going down!

02:04.102 --> 02:07.730
I can't believe this. She keeps getting up.
I'm so exhausted.

02:10.652 --> 02:15.072
And the winner, by technical knockout,
weighing in at 67 pounds,

02:15.155 --> 02:18.619
Carol "Put On Your Sunday Clothes"
Channing.

02:18.743 --> 02:19.786
Yeah.

02:20.746 --> 02:22.581
Up yours, young people.

02:22.790 --> 02:25.878
You and your rock and roll 8-track tapes!

02:25.961 --> 02:28.671
I don't believe this. I just lost a $50 bet.

02:28.797 --> 02:31.258
You know,
Mike Tyson once beat up his wife.

02:31.384 --> 02:33.928
But there's nothing funny about that.

02:36.598 --> 02:40.226
- Hi, guys. We're back from the mall.
- I got new shoes.

02:40.309 --> 02:42.479
The old ones are in the box.

02:43.355 --> 02:45.316
They smell and are old.

02:45.816 --> 02:49.029
Hey, Peter, your 25th high-school reunion
is next Sunday.

02:49.153 --> 02:50.947
Throw that away. I don't want to go.

02:51.030 --> 02:53.074
Besides, Sunday's my Internet porn night.

02:54.660 --> 02:56.245
Oh, yeah!

02:56.536 --> 02:59.040
You're my Chinese Lois.

03:02.042 --> 03:03.920
Hey, it's me. Knock, knock.

03:04.004 --> 03:08.675
- So, you got my money?
- Oh, yeah. I'll pay you soon.

03:08.800 --> 03:11.095
Yeah, well, here's a suggestion.

03:11.345 --> 03:14.433
Have the money by tomorrow,
and there won't be any problems.

03:14.515 --> 03:16.184
- Huh?
- Yeah, 24 hours.

03:16.310 --> 03:18.062
Why? What happens in 24 hours?

03:18.187 --> 03:20.105
I don't know. I'm not psychic, man.

03:20.188 --> 03:22.275
I'm just saying it would probably be
better for everybody

03:22.358 --> 03:23.984
- if you had the money tomorrow.
- Yeah, all right.

03:24.068 --> 03:27.072
- I'll see what I can do.
- Sweet, sweet. Great.

03:27.281 --> 03:28.614
- How's everything else going?
- Good.

03:28.698 --> 03:31.701
All right. All right, see you later.
Don't forget.

03:32.285 --> 03:33.663
No, you're not gonna forget.

03:36.707 --> 03:38.209
Hey, Peter, I was going through
your garbage,

03:38.334 --> 03:40.253
and I noticed your high-school
reunion is coming up.

03:40.379 --> 03:41.629
Why were you going through my garbage?

03:41.712 --> 03:44.342
Well, when I stopped over earlier,
I noticed Lois clipping her toenails,

03:44.467 --> 03:46.093
and I thought,
"Oh, man, I got to get in on that. "

03:46.218 --> 03:47.219
Huh.

03:47.345 --> 03:49.347
Yeah, I don't think
I'm going to my reunion.

03:49.472 --> 03:52.685
Everybody's all got their nice cars,
and their big, important jobs,

03:52.810 --> 03:55.729
and their fancy hats,
and their fresh strawberries

03:55.813 --> 03:58.064
so big you can eat them like a hand fruit.

03:58.189 --> 04:01.820
Peter, everyone lies at those things.
Just tell them you're a big shot.

04:01.904 --> 04:04.239
Wait a second, Joe, that's a great idea.

04:04.364 --> 04:06.867
Boy, imagine what it would be like
to be a big shot.

04:10.705 --> 04:13.500
Diego? Sweaty.

04:15.835 --> 04:16.879
Thank you.

04:24.720 --> 04:28.892
- Stewie, hey.
- Hey, there. So, it's been 24 hours.

04:28.976 --> 04:30.727
- Got my money?
- You know what?

04:30.853 --> 04:33.398
Just give me till next Friday.
I'll have it for you.

04:33.523 --> 04:36.025
That's funny.
I could have sworn I said have it today.

04:36.108 --> 04:39.237
- Yeah, I don't have it, sorry.
- Well. All right, then.

04:40.114 --> 04:41.782
That's good OJ.

04:43.826 --> 04:46.162
- Yeah, that hurt? That hurt?
- What the hell?

04:46.288 --> 04:48.790
Yeah, doesn't feel so good, does it? No?

04:51.085 --> 04:53.587
- Yeah, that's what happens, man.
- Oh, my God.

04:53.796 --> 04:54.755
Yeah, that's what happens.

04:56.424 --> 04:57.758
Where's my money?

04:58.593 --> 05:01.513
You gonna give me my money?
Where's my money, man?

05:04.140 --> 05:05.600
Where's the money?

05:07.519 --> 05:10.398
Yeah, you like that? That feel good?
That feel good?

05:12.525 --> 05:14.902
Where's the money, man?
Where's my money?

05:18.200 --> 05:21.618
You've got till 5:00. You hear me?
You got till 5:00.

05:21.702 --> 05:24.498
- You freaking psychopath!
- Clean yourself up.

05:31.797 --> 05:34.508
Peter, this is ridiculous.
Why can't you just be yourself?

05:34.634 --> 05:37.053
Lois, just go along with it.
Act like I'm a big shot.

05:38.597 --> 05:42.476
- Hey, Peter Griffin, is that you?
- Hey, Mike, long time no see.

05:42.601 --> 05:44.019
Wow. What...

05:44.144 --> 05:46.524
- What's all this?
- This? I just came from work.

05:46.606 --> 05:50.944
- I'm a secret agent astronaut millionaire.
- Cool. Where'd you get the cowboy hat?

05:51.988 --> 05:54.865
- Space.
- By the way, this is my friend, Tom.

05:55.407 --> 05:57.994
You're Tom Brady
from the New England Patriots!

05:58.120 --> 06:00.288
Oh, man, I got to tell you,
you kick ass, man.

06:00.372 --> 06:01.956
In fact, I was just saying
that the other day

06:02.040 --> 06:03.542
to all the guys down at the brewery.

06:03.625 --> 06:06.462
Brewery? I thought you were
a cowboy astronaut millionaire.

06:06.671 --> 06:09.757
He's a fake!
Look, this cowboy hat comes right off.

06:14.429 --> 06:17.100
Coming here was a huge mistake, Lois.

06:17.225 --> 06:20.603
Peter, I know you're humiliated,
but getting drunk is not the answer.

06:20.727 --> 06:24.859
Uh-oh. Either my esophagus just
got shorter, or I'm about to throw up.

06:32.991 --> 06:34.662
Peter, that was amazing.

06:34.744 --> 06:37.039
I've never seen a guy your size
who could move like that.

06:37.165 --> 06:40.208
How would you like to play
for the New England Patriots?

06:40.667 --> 06:41.794
I'd love to.

06:42.253 --> 06:43.378
Say, listen, Tom,

06:43.462 --> 06:45.424
could you get me a towel?
I threw up on the floor.

06:45.548 --> 06:46.550
Sure.

06:46.676 --> 06:48.718
And could you also get another towel?

06:48.843 --> 06:50.888
I also threw up
on this gentleman's bare lap.

06:50.970 --> 06:52.723
Could you wet the towel?
- Wet the towel, Tom?

06:55.226 --> 06:58.647
For our top story tonight,
we go live to terrific haircut Bob Costas

06:58.772 --> 07:00.815
as he talks with local man Peter Griffin,

07:00.940 --> 07:03.402
who is living his dream of playing
for the New England Patriots.

07:03.486 --> 07:04.570
- Bob?
- Thanks, Tom.

07:04.654 --> 07:06.072
I'm fond of your hair, as well.

07:06.155 --> 07:09.784
I'm standing here with Tom Brady
and his newest teammate, Peter Griffin.

07:09.910 --> 07:13.205
Hey, Ma! Check it out!
I'm married to a pro athlete!

07:13.289 --> 07:14.832
What do you think of that?

07:16.291 --> 07:17.626
We're really excited to have Peter.

07:17.751 --> 07:20.213
I think he's gonna make a great addition
to a great team.

07:20.296 --> 07:23.467
I want to thank God.
I want to thank the Lord God.

07:24.133 --> 07:26.804
'Cause it's not really up to me.
It's up to him.

07:27.679 --> 07:29.723
And I want to thank the devil, too.

07:29.806 --> 07:32.936
You know, 'cause that's why God's there.

07:33.145 --> 07:36.773
He's minding the fence,
making sure that guy never comes back.

07:37.274 --> 07:38.232
Uh...

07:38.608 --> 07:40.985
You know, if it weren't for the devil,
God'd probably go insane,

07:41.112 --> 07:43.906
blow his brains out from boredom,
you know?

07:44.657 --> 07:49.370
Everybody likes to feel useful.
Maketh the world go round.

07:49.954 --> 07:51.040
Back to you, Tom.

07:51.164 --> 07:53.292
Diane, didn't your first husband
blow his brains out?

07:53.376 --> 07:55.337
Oh, God.

07:56.879 --> 07:59.925
Coming up, America's hottest new
curse word, "kleeman. "

08:00.008 --> 08:01.802
We'll tell you what it means after this.

08:01.886 --> 08:04.054
Boy, Lois, I can't believe
this is happening to me.

08:04.180 --> 08:05.889
I'm somebody now, you know?

08:06.014 --> 08:08.852
I don't have to lie to people
about my life anymore.

08:08.934 --> 08:11.479
Oh, I am so happy for you, Peter.

08:11.855 --> 08:13.732
What the hell happened to you?

08:14.566 --> 08:16.860
I fell down the stairs.

08:16.985 --> 08:18.320
Oh, you should be more careful.

08:21.033 --> 08:23.033
All right, I'm ready. Come on, good game.

08:23.159 --> 08:24.953
Good game, everybody. Yeah.
Come on, good game.

08:25.037 --> 08:29.417
Let's get out there. Let's do it. Yeah, yeah.
110%, everybody. 110%.

08:29.543 --> 08:31.837
Come on, let's go. Let's go. Good game!

08:32.879 --> 08:36.258
Ready! Blue 20, blue 20! Hut, hut!

08:36.508 --> 08:39.387
- Griffin, let go!
- Let's go?

08:59.077 --> 09:01.035
- Morning.
- Good day to you, sir.

09:01.119 --> 09:02.286
Hey, wait a minute. What the hell?

09:09.796 --> 09:12.633
Getting real tired of you ducking me,
man. Yeah?

09:12.757 --> 09:15.553
- Oh, my God!
- Yeah, getting really tired.

09:19.473 --> 09:21.768
Where's my money? Where's my money?

09:23.019 --> 09:26.232
Yeah, you got money to pay
for fake mustaches, huh? Yeah.

09:26.316 --> 09:28.568
Yeah, how much you pay
for that fake mustache?

09:28.692 --> 09:29.652
$2.99.

09:33.240 --> 09:35.408
Listen, you just got to give me
more time...

09:35.533 --> 09:38.330
Don't make a fool out of me, man.
Don't make a fool out of me.

09:38.454 --> 09:41.581
I want my money.
I want my money, man.

09:41.665 --> 09:44.627
Stewie, listen, this is crazy. You got...
Oh, my God.

09:50.968 --> 09:52.470
All right, let's go to the bank.

09:55.182 --> 09:58.351
Well, I got to tell you,
this was a delicious dinner, Mrs. Griffin.

09:59.269 --> 10:02.773
- Well, the pleasure is all ours, Mr. Brady.
- Please, call me Tom.

10:05.110 --> 10:07.570
- Can I call you Tom, too?
- Well, of course.

10:09.990 --> 10:12.867
Mr. Brady, would you please sign
my Trapper Keeper?

10:13.075 --> 10:16.455
Oh, Tom, your shirt. I'm so sorry.

10:16.539 --> 10:19.292
- Look, you can use our shower if you want.
- No, it's okay.

10:19.417 --> 10:21.377
It's just a little spot. It'll come out.

10:21.502 --> 10:24.506
Well, that's not gonna come out.
You better take a shower.

10:30.096 --> 10:33.015
- Mom, let me look!
- Meg, stop shoving.

10:33.098 --> 10:34.644
You wouldn't even know
what to do with it.

10:34.728 --> 10:36.728
He's closer to my age, you cow.

10:37.563 --> 10:39.983
- What the hell is this?
- Oh, hi, Stewie.

10:40.107 --> 10:42.902
- We were just leaving.
- I say, what the devil is all the fuss about?

10:43.027 --> 10:45.988
I don't get it. What's in there?
Bing, bong! Hello!

10:48.033 --> 10:51.120
- Hey. What's going on?
- What the hell? Get out of here!

10:51.204 --> 10:53.247
What? We're on the same team.
We shower together.

10:53.372 --> 10:55.417
- Yeah, in the locker room.
- Yeah, yeah, come here, you.

10:55.542 --> 10:57.543
Stop it. Knock it off. What, are you crazy?

10:57.668 --> 10:59.588
We're just a couple of guys
messing around.

10:59.712 --> 11:00.672
That's what we are.

11:02.384 --> 11:04.511
Quiet, everybody, my commercial's on.

11:04.719 --> 11:07.848
<i>Hi, I'm Peter Griffin
of the New England Patriots.</i>

11:07.971 --> 11:10.976
<i>I'm here to kick off the Touchdown
of Savings weekend</i>

11:11.059 --> 11:13.479
<i>at Wilkins Hyundai and Subaru.</i>

11:13.896 --> 11:16.899
<i>We will blitz the competition,
and in no time,</i>

11:17.108 --> 11:21.738
<i>you'll be driving your new Hyundai
or Subaru right to a touchdown.</i>

11:32.250 --> 11:35.421
Mom, the game's about to start.
Where's Dad?

11:35.546 --> 11:38.215
I don't know, Chris.
And I'm starting to get worried.

11:38.341 --> 11:40.970
I think all this success
might be going to his head.

11:41.095 --> 11:44.055
Do you know he spent
$30,000 on a wax sculpture

11:44.138 --> 11:46.640
of Harriet Tubman
doing Gwyneth Paltrow?

11:47.475 --> 11:50.773
Yeah. Yeah,
that is happening for real. Yeah.

11:50.897 --> 11:51.857
Yeah.

11:53.275 --> 11:55.193
I'll enjoy that more tomorrow.

11:55.944 --> 11:58.405
Where the hell is Griffin?
It's almost time for kickoff.

11:58.488 --> 12:00.617
Well, I guess we have
to start without him.

12:06.455 --> 12:09.835
What do you think?
I got this for doing that car dealership ad.

12:09.960 --> 12:12.379
All right, enough messing around.
Let's play this game.

12:12.463 --> 12:14.256
Let's play some football.

12:14.339 --> 12:16.800
Griffin, I'm getting really tired
of your cocky attitude.

12:16.884 --> 12:19.055
How many times have I told you,
no showboating?

12:19.137 --> 12:22.600
Relax, Tom, I'm just having a little fun.
I got it under control.

12:22.684 --> 12:26.937
Okay, 28-Z right, pitch left, on one, on one.
Ready? Break!

12:27.939 --> 12:31.693
Ready, green 54! Green 54! Set, hut, hut!

12:40.412 --> 12:41.455
Yeah!

12:42.664 --> 12:44.583
There might be some hope
for this guy after all.

12:44.667 --> 12:45.667
Yeah.

12:47.044 --> 12:49.631
Damn it, Griffin! I said no showboating!

12:49.797 --> 12:51.883
This calls for a victory tune!

14:28.534 --> 14:30.287
No! No!

15:12.043 --> 15:15.088
All right. I made a touchdown.

15:15.338 --> 15:18.215
- Griffin, you're fired!
- For what?

15:18.341 --> 15:19.509
We've had it with your crap.

15:19.635 --> 15:22.637
I talked to the coach, and
he's selling your contract to another team.

15:22.763 --> 15:26.101
And the only one that'll take you
is the worst football team in Europe,

15:26.184 --> 15:28.018
the London Silly Nannies.

15:33.192 --> 15:36.946
So, Brian, we're even now, right?
Ready to start a new life in England.

15:37.029 --> 15:39.240
I've got my money.
Your wounds have healed up nicely.

15:39.365 --> 15:41.327
What do you say
we let bygones be bygones?

15:41.452 --> 15:45.372
You shot me in both my knees,
then lit me on fire. Piss off.

15:45.497 --> 15:47.249
All right, all right. I tell you what,

15:47.374 --> 15:50.211
- you get one free revenge shot at me.
- Okay.

15:50.462 --> 15:52.881
But I'm not gonna tell you
when it's coming.

15:57.302 --> 15:59.013
This is gonna be fun.

15:59.222 --> 16:00.682
Peter, this is crazy.

16:00.807 --> 16:03.893
Isn't there any way the Patriots
could let you back on the team?

16:04.019 --> 16:06.021
No, they said the decision was final.

16:06.146 --> 16:08.107
It's all right, Lois.
I can make the best of this.

16:08.233 --> 16:10.443
I mean, a British football team
can't be that bad.

16:12.736 --> 16:16.741
Excuse me. Hey, there.
Hi. I'm Peter Griffin. I'm your new player.

16:16.867 --> 16:19.203
Oh, yes, Peter.
Welcome to the Silly Nannies.

16:19.328 --> 16:21.915
I'm the quarterback, Lesley.
This is our team.

16:40.311 --> 16:41.686
Oh, crap.

16:46.149 --> 16:49.488
I guess living in a London flat
isn't gonna be too bad, huh?

16:49.696 --> 16:54.243
- Mom, there's no water in the toilet.
- First of all, Chris, it's called a loo.

16:54.326 --> 16:55.577
Second, there's no water in it,

16:55.661 --> 16:58.372
because everybody here
just uses Elizabeth Hurley.

16:58.456 --> 17:01.084
All right, well, where is she?
'Cause I need her now!

17:02.711 --> 17:04.420
<i>You're watching BBC FOUR.</i>

17:04.630 --> 17:06.799
<i>Previously on Condensation.</i>

17:07.091 --> 17:10.094
<i>Ellen, there's moisture
on the outside of my glass.</i>

17:10.261 --> 17:14.724
<i>- It's condensation, Johnny.
- But what about the fog on the windows?</i>

17:14.807 --> 17:19.271
<i>It's not fog, Johnny.
It, too, is called condensation.</i>

17:19.564 --> 17:22.608
<i>'"Con-den-sation. '"</i>

17:24.402 --> 17:27.364
Hey, Peter, how was your first
Silly Nannies practice?

17:27.489 --> 17:28.783
It sucked, Lois.

17:28.908 --> 17:31.284
Those Silly Nannies
are just a bunch of losers.

17:31.368 --> 17:34.290
- Pack your bags. We're going home.
- What, you're just giving up?

17:34.373 --> 17:37.542
Look, Peter, I know you're upset
because you blew your opportunity

17:37.667 --> 17:39.211
with the Patriots.

17:39.503 --> 17:41.964
But this is your chance to redeem yourself.

17:42.172 --> 17:45.385
Now, I bet if you really tried,
you could turn that team around.

17:45.510 --> 17:46.761
You know what, Lois?

17:46.845 --> 17:49.598
When you were talking about that sale
at TJ Maxx just now,

17:49.680 --> 17:51.099
I came up with an idea.

17:51.183 --> 17:53.311
I am going to turn that team around.

17:53.394 --> 17:57.147
And we'll challenge the Patriots to a game,
and we'll kick their ass!

17:59.817 --> 18:01.528
Oh, man, what an attractive woman.

18:02.821 --> 18:05.282
- Hello?
- Hey, Brady, you're dead!

18:05.366 --> 18:07.994
Listen, Leno, you keep calling here
and threatening me,

18:08.076 --> 18:10.120
- I'm gonna notify the police.
- Leno?

18:10.204 --> 18:11.413
No, no, this is Peter Griffin.

18:11.539 --> 18:13.834
I'm calling to challenge you
to a grudge match

18:13.916 --> 18:17.046
between the Patriots
and the London Silly Nannies.

18:17.337 --> 18:20.299
Well, Griffin, if you want to embarrass
yourself, be my guest.

18:20.382 --> 18:23.220
Good. What do you say, England?
Two weeks from now?

18:23.387 --> 18:24.554
See you there.

18:26.222 --> 18:27.516
- Hello?
- Hey, Brady!

18:27.641 --> 18:30.102
What kind of suit
do you want to be buried in?

18:38.402 --> 18:40.030
You kids are gonna love this.

18:40.155 --> 18:42.533
England has such a rich heritage
of great theater.

18:44.410 --> 18:46.329
Cramsat on the bingum
with the gam gum?

18:46.413 --> 18:48.873
Treaches on the upper
with the trang sang.

18:49.749 --> 18:52.210
Croppers to you, you crang sang lubber.

18:55.006 --> 18:56.632
She rogered the boogley!

18:59.969 --> 19:02.515
All right, now listen up,
you limey bum sniffers.

19:02.599 --> 19:04.725
If we're gonna beat
the New England Patriots next week,

19:04.850 --> 19:06.101
I got to toughen you up.

19:06.227 --> 19:09.062
So you're gonna get in shape
the way American athletes do,

19:09.146 --> 19:10.857
by taking steroids.

19:10.940 --> 19:13.861
I say, Jenkins, you give me
that dirty look one more time,

19:14.028 --> 19:17.281
and I've a good mind to get into my PJ's
and have a pillow fight with you.

19:17.406 --> 19:19.075
Very well, then. En garde!

19:21.076 --> 19:22.496
- I like your gown.
- I like yours.

19:31.172 --> 19:34.551
When's the beating gonna come, Brian?
Just tell me when it's gonna come!

19:34.634 --> 19:37.678
Just do something, anything!
Look, look, I'll do it. I'll do it first.

19:37.803 --> 19:40.391
Look, I'll do it even worse.

19:41.601 --> 19:43.185
Look how hurt I am.

19:43.978 --> 19:45.438
We're even now!

19:50.361 --> 19:54.115
- You're going down, Brady!
- You're the one who's going down, Griffin!

19:54.489 --> 19:55.741
What the hell?

20:03.333 --> 20:07.547
- Those men are tremendous in stature.
- And they're coming straight at us!

20:07.672 --> 20:08.632
Oh!

20:11.134 --> 20:12.719
We'll take my carriage.

20:16.182 --> 20:17.266
Oh, crap!

20:17.350 --> 20:20.478
Well, I'm still here, you bastards,
so let's do this.

20:26.944 --> 20:30.448
Hey, Brady, you're gonna gloat
and call me a loser now?

20:30.532 --> 20:32.617
Actually, Peter, you're not a loser at all.

20:32.700 --> 20:35.328
- What you did just now was pretty ballsy.
- Really?

20:35.453 --> 20:37.665
Absolutely! For one guy

20:37.747 --> 20:40.292
to stand up
to the entire New England Patriots team.

20:40.376 --> 20:42.169
That's a winner in my book.

20:44.546 --> 20:46.341
Wow. Thanks, Tom Brady.

20:47.551 --> 20:50.262
- Peter! Oh, my God, are you all right?
- Yeah.

20:50.388 --> 20:52.265
- Can you move your legs?
- Yeah!

20:52.390 --> 20:55.143
Oh, good.
I thought you were gonna be a vegetable,

20:55.227 --> 20:59.230
and I gotta tell you, Peter,
I just don't think I have it in me.

20:59.731 --> 21:01.775
I mean, if you can't move, it's over.

21:01.900 --> 21:05.113
I love you, too, honey. Let's go home.

21:05.114 --> 22:06.114
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru